==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
* From {{suf|en|elastic|ance}}.
* {{sense|physics}} Coined by {{w|Oliver Heaviside}}. There is a force–voltage {{w|Mechanical–electrical analogies|electromechanical analogy}} in which capacitance corresponds to the inverse of a [[spring constant]]; the smaller the spring constant, the more “elastic” (yielding, flexible) the spring is.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|physics}} An [[electrical]] [[property]] that is the [[inverse]] of [[capacitance]].
# {{lb|en|mechanics}} The [[inverse]] of [[compliance]].
# {{lb|en|medicine}} A measurement of the tendency of the [[lung]], [[urinary]] [[bladder]], [[gallbladder]] or other [[cavity]] to recoil inwards.
#: {{ant|en|compliance}}

